# =============================================================================
# Mol-Metal .gitignore
# Targets a PUBLIC release: ~50 MB of source + load-bearing reports + tiny
# checkpoints. Heavy items below are EXCLUDED — see README §11.6 (datasets)
# and §11.7 (checkpoints) for re-acquisition instructions.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python bytecode & venv -------------------------------------------------
# .venv/ is the CANONICAL Mol-Metal environment (AGENTS.md §5.9 single-venv
# rule: the repo-local .venv is THE interpreter; the legacy CadButEaas /
# kanzi venvs are forbidden). It is ignored because environments are never
# committed — not because it is stale. The guard at
# molmetal/scripts/check_no_stale_venv.sh fails if the repo is pointed at
# any interpreter other than this .venv.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# --- LaTeX build artefacts (paper/main.pdf is the only tracked output) ------
**/*.aux
**/*.bbl
**/*.blg
**/*.log
**/*.toc
**/*.fls
**/*.fdb_latexmk
**/*.synctex.gz
**/*.nav
**/*.out
**/*.snm
**/*.vrb
**/*.dvi
paper/main.pdf

# --- Heavy cloned SOTA repos (3.57 GB; clone per molmetal/references/README.md)
molmetal/references/
!molmetal/references/README.md
!molmetal/references/clone_all.sh

# --- Wf-253-A: exclude top-level reference clones + transient cache dirs ----
# These are local working clones + training cache; not source.
references/
.cloned/
.ckpt/
# Chemprop pre-computed molecular graph cache (regenerated by build script)
molmetal/data/chemprop_features/
# Large pre-featurized datasets (regenerated by build_cache.py)
molmetal/data/pre_featurized/
# Chemprop feature .npz caches
**/chemprop_features/**/*.npz
molmetal/reports/**/*.npz
molmetal/reports/**/cache/
molmetal/reports/**/__pycache__/

# --- Top-level transient workflow output -----------------------------------
# These are working artefacts from past ultracode workflows; not source.
_a1_sanity.py
conftest.py
cutoff_sweep.json
cutoff_sweep.md
texput.log
topo_plot.png
topo_plot_clean.png
%{size_download}\n
wf_lambda_mcts_coords_fix/
workflow-scripts/
# Wf-449 state-locking runtime lock files (per AGENTS.md §5.6 atomic write
# protocol — prevent concurrent trainer invocations on the same yaml; not
# source).
configs/training/.state/

# --- Pre-trained model checkpoints (large; SHIPPED via `git add -f`) --------
# Default policy: include molmetal/checkpoints/ (canonical, 70 MB)
# for paper §4 Table 1 reproducibility.
# Top-level checkpoints/ contains pre-R12 legacy models (model.pt +
# learned_prior_Pt.*) which are superseded by molmetal/checkpoints/*.pt.
# fpscores.pkl.gz is regenerable via sascorer.py's pickle download path.
# To exclude all checkpoints (reduce repo size), uncomment the next 3 lines:
# molmetal/checkpoints/
# checkpoints/
# molmetal/eval/scoring/fpscores.pkl.gz
# Keep these (canonical pretrained for paper §4 Table 1 reproducibility):
#   molmetal/checkpoints/fm_pocket.pt  fm_pocket_conditioned.pt  fm_ru_temporal.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/metal_hybrid_v4_{ru_temporal,mb1}_seed{42,133,256}.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/dmpnn_attn_ru_pic50.pt  dmpnn_tmqm_pretrained.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/dmpnn_attn_heLa48h_dark_retrained.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/egnn_tmqm_finetuned_ru.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/metal_hybrid_{Ru,v1,v2,v3}_*.pt
#   molmetal/checkpoints/metallo_drug_smoke_mol_cache.pt
checkpoints/
molmetal/eval/scoring/fpscores.pkl.gz

# --- Heavy data (NOT shipped; download per README §11.6) --------------------
/mnt/storage/
data/qm9_raw/
data/qm9_processed.pt
data/crossdocked/
data/tmQM/
data/platinai/
data/cytotox/
data/nci60/

# --- Heavy / transient workflow artefacts in reports/ -----------------------
# Workflow artefacts tier policy:
#   TIER A (tracked):  *.md, *.tex, small JSON (final.json, MASTER.json, summary.json)
#   TIER B (ignored):  PNG plots, raw train logs, large JSON dumps, ckpt.pt,
#                      docking poses (regenerable), raw CSV probes
molmetal/reports/**/*.png
molmetal/reports/**/*.csv
molmetal/reports/**/*.pt
molmetal/reports/**/*.pkl
molmetal/reports/**/*.npy
molmetal/reports/**/train.log
molmetal/reports/**/ckpt.pt
molmetal/reports/**/decode_smoke_*.json
molmetal/reports/**/*poses*/
molmetal/reports/**/*_poses/
molmetal/reports/**/*_docked*/
molmetal/reports/**/receptor.json
molmetal/reports/**/receptor.pdbqt
molmetal/reports/**/*.tar.gz
molmetal/reports/**/*.zip
# Large JSON dumps (>500 KB) — raw machine-readable runs; load-bearing small
# JSONs (final.json, verdict.json, summary.json ≤ 100 KB) ARE tracked.
molmetal/reports/**/*.json
!molmetal/reports/**/final.json
!molmetal/reports/**/final.md
!molmetal/reports/**/MASTER.md
!molmetal/reports/**/verdict.md
!molmetal/reports/**/summary.md
!molmetal/reports/**/final_small.json
!molmetal/reports/**/summary_small.json
# Wf-30 Phase 4 load-bearing analysis (small, MEASURED, source of truth)
!molmetal/reports/wf30_dock/m3_lift_analysis.json
!molmetal/reports/wf30_dock/m3_lift_summary.md
# Wf-44 Phase 2 baseline check (small, source of truth for R² debug)
!molmetal/reports/wf44_r2_debug/baseline_check.json
!molmetal/reports/wf44_r2_debug/root_cause_catalog.md
!molmetal/reports/wf44_r2_debug/root_cause_checklist.json

# --- Joblib caches (rebuilt by build_cache.py) ------------------------------
molmetal/molmetal_lam/tile_lib/.cache/

# --- Jupyter ---------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

# --- Local override / runtime files -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.local
*.tmp
*.bak
core
core.*

# --- Claude-code / agent meta (LOCAL only, do NOT ship) ---------------------
.claude/

# --- Local dataset cache (per-host symlinks + downloaded corpora) ----------
#   DATA_STATUS.md at the project root IS tracked (dataset inventory doc);
#   everything else under .data/ is host-specific.
.data/molmetal/
.data/cache/
*.venv*

# --- Commit-path gate output (H1 / HOLE-8 fix, 2026-10-03) -------------------
# These paths are REWRITTEN by molmetal/scripts/pre_flight_check.py's
# build_gates("all") commit-path pipeline on every hook run (the wf385 gate
# re-runs the real trainer; the hp-provenance gate rewrites the JSONL). They
# are runtime gate output, not source: kept on disk per AGENTS.md §5.5 but
# untracked so a commit can never record a transient gate write, and
# regenerated by the first gate run in a fresh clone.
# See TODO/completed/h1_precommit_holes_3_8.md for the pending redirect
# follow-up in pre_flight_check.py (contested file, not edited by H1).
molmetal/reports/wf350a3_hp_provenance.jsonl
molmetal/reports/wf385a3_scaffold_wire_in/train/
# Reserved scratch root for that pending redirect (pre_flight_check.py
# default out_dir); ignored now so the follow-up cannot re-dirty the tree.
results/gate_scratch/

# --- Wf-A16 (2026-10-03): accidental artifacts, purged in this wave ---------
# MEASURED: `--help` and `--output-dir` were TRACKED for weeks. They are the
# same audit run written twice, 4 s apart (differing only in a timestamp), i.e.
# a command whose output was redirected onto its own flag names. The real report
# is molmetal/reports/wf65_p1_sign_audit/sign_flip_audit.json.
/--help
/--output-dir
.pytest_tmp/
# Migration backups. These duplicate content that is either in git history or
# superseded; 77 of them had accumulated as tracked files.
*.bak.*
